codex
The root cause is now concrete: this audit sandbox reports a PID that has no `/proc/<pid>/exe`, while `/proc/self/exe` works. Lean 4.22’s `IO.appPath` uses the former and therefore fails before elaboration. I’m applying a narrowly scoped runtime compatibility shim in `/tmp/audit-work` that redirects only `/proc/<digits>/exe` reads to `/proc/self/exe`; it does not alter candidate/generated sources or Lean’s kernel/trust behavior.
apply patch
